{
  "slug": "sdd-superpowers",
  "name": "Sdd Superpowers",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Specification-Driven Development (SDD) for Claude Code: write specs first, generate code from them. 9-skill workflow covering brainstorm → specify → research → plan → tasks → execute → update → review",
  "longDescription": "Ships **21 skills**, **1 agent** and **5 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (21): `dispatching-parallel-agents` (Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies), `finishing-a-development-branch` (Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and a decision is needed on how to integrate the…), `receiving-code-review` (Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing review suggestions), `requesting-code-review` (Use when completing a development phase or major feature, and before merging to main), `sdd-brainstorm` (Use when an idea is fuzzy, exploratory, or has competing approaches that need design exploration before specification), `sdd-execute` (Use when a plan is approved and implementation should begin), `sdd-init` (Use when starting a new project that has no CLAUDE.md and no docs/specs/ directory), `sdd-plan` (Use when a feature spec exists and needs to become a technical implementation plan), and 13 more\n- **Agents** (1): `code-reviewer` (Use this agent when a major project step has been completed and needs to be reviewed against the…)\n- **Hooks** (5): `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `SubagentStart`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install sdd-superpowers@claude-community` from `hllj/sdd-superpowers`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 21,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 5
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
